## The problem

Commercial reverse vending machines cost $6,500 to $25,000 because they stack barcode scanners, spectrometers and weight sensors. That price keeps them out of countries like Pakistan.

## The approach

One camera and one detector replace the sensor stack. An IR trigger takes a still frame, YOLO11n classifies it, and the STM32 drives the sort or reject gate.

## The surprise

Newer is not faster. On a CPU, YOLO11n beat both YOLOv12 and YOLO26 on latency and energy.
